(vector (map (:adr/consequences "{:milestones \"M4 murakumo chat live (retarget + secret decision + first live\\n               verification incl. structured-output question) -> M5 avatars -> M6 kisekae\\n               flow embed -> M7 LP restructure; M4/M5 independent\", :open_items [\"murakumo bridge's ANTHROPIC_PROXY_TOKEN production state\" \"qwen model's JSON-contract fidelity\" \"kotobase-backed SpecStore + account identity\"], :new_deps \"net-babiniku gains kotoba-lang/kisekae, canvaskit, editor (sibling\\n             :local/root) when M6 lands\", :adr_amendment \"ADR-2607070800 amended in place: provider superseded, boundary retained\", :addendum_2607080800 {:context \"M6's compose engine (ADR-2607071610, shipped and verified live) closes\\n             the '2 missing character avatars' open item without any new\\n             third-party asset\", :closed {:what \"jk-luxury/net-babiniku#39: rin and mei get real avatars composed from\\n           the SAME two already-licensed VRM Consortium sample files aoi/yui\\n           already use -- rin = VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample body + Seed-san\\n           hair/outfit; mei = Seed-san body/outfit + VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample\\n           hair/face (Twist-Sample has no separate :outfit category to donate)\", :license_basis \"checked directly against both files' embedded VRMC_vrm.meta,\\n                    not assumed -- both declare modification:\\n                    allowModificationRedistribution, avatarPermission: everyone,\\n                    allowRedistribution: true under VRM Public License 1.0\"}, :compliance_gap_also_fixed {:what \"Seed-san's creditNotation is 'required' (credit VirtualCast, Inc.) but\\n           nothing in the app credited it anywhere for aoi's existing avatar\\n           either -- a real, previously-missing gap, not hypothetical\", :fix \"every built-in character now carries :avatar-credit, rendered\\n         unconditionally and visibly on its card, not tucked in a collapsed\\n         details block\"}, :design_note \":avatar-spec (built-in characters only) kept SEPARATE from\\n                 :kisekae/spec (user-created characters) so character-card-view's\\n                 created? check stays correctly scoped -- rin/mei get real\\n                 composed avatars without gaining Edit/Export/Delete UI meant only\\n                 for what a visitor actually created\", :verification \"verified live in production: both avatars render as full,\\n                  correctly-posed, distinct humanoids; no console errors; full nbb\\n                  test suite (character/governor/monetization/embodiment/persona)\\n                  passes\"}}"), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "net-babiniku's 完成系 is five capabilities with explicit done-criteria: live chat\n    (murakumo), live per-character avatars, character creation (kisekae), visitor-shaped\n    LP, and monetization staying honestly HARD-held until the etzhayyim rail matures" "the LLM backend targets api.murakumo.cloud/v1/messages (local-murakumo, verified\n    self-hosted qwen-agentworld-35b-a3b, no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY anywhere) -- NOT the\n    murakumo.cloud Sora proxy, whose upstream is unverifiable and could silently be real\n    Anthropic; ADR-2607070800 is superseded in provider/model choice only, its boundary\n    design (server-side call, persona prompts, schema-mirrors-governor, honest-default)\n    carries forward" "per-character avatars port network-isekai's isekai.stage avatar-cache/ensure-avatar!\n    pattern; roster gains :vrm-url; only 2 license-clear sample VRMs exist, which is why\n    kisekae-produced user avatars are the durable supply" "character creation embeds the kisekae flow (ADR-2607071610): spec-as-artifact,\n    MemSpecStore first, kotobase-backed persistence as follow-up wiring; created\n    characters are the creator-economy supply side of ADR-2607062200's 80/20" "the LP re-frames containment transparency as a labeled trust section -- nothing about\n    the audit-ledger design is deleted")), (:adr/supersedes (vector "adr-2607070800 (provider/model choice only)")), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "net-babiniku-service-completion"), (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607071610-kotoba-lang-kisekae-vrm-character-editor.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607070800-net-babiniku-llm-backend-claude-sonnet-5.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607071000-net-babiniku-crypto-payment-rail-etzhayyim-consumption.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607062200-net-babiniku-onlyfans-style-creator-monetization.edn")), (:adr/status "proposed"), (:adr/id "adr-2607071600-net-babiniku-service-completion-design"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-07"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607071600: net-babiniku 完成系 — service completion design (LP, live avatars, murakumo LLM, kisekae editor)\n\n## Status\nProposed (design accepted by user direction 2026-07-07 \"do it\"; individual milestones land as their own PRs against this map)\n\n## Context\n\nUser direction (2026-07-07): \"babiniku.net の lp なども含めて、サービスとして完成系を設計して、\nまた vrm character editor なども kotoba-lang として、ユーザーが使いやすいものを再設計して.\nkotoba wasm, cljc, kotobase datomic\" — design the *finished* service, LP included, plus a\nuser-friendly VRM character editor as a kotoba-lang library (that editor is ADR-2607071610,\n`kotoba-lang/kisekae`; this ADR is the service that consumes it). Two earlier same-session\ndirectives fold in: \"anthropic key はつかわずに murakumo.cloud を使って\" (drop the direct\nAnthropic key, use murakumo.cloud), and the observation that the deployed page shows \"単なる\n四角いオブジェクト\" (just a box) where an avatar should be.\n\n### Where the product actually stands (Milestones 0–3, all deployed)\n\nThe containment architecture is real and tested (`babiniku.governor` HARD/SOFT gate +\nescalation, `babiniku.monetization` honest-default HARD-hold, `babiniku.embodiment`\nOtete-only gate, 65 nbb checks) and a real chat pipeline exists end-to-end (persona system\nprompts, structured-output schema, per-character transcripts, conversation history, thinking\nindicator — PRs #15–#21). But as a *service* it is incomplete in exactly four ways:\n\n1. **No live LLM** — `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` was never provisioned; every chat returns the\n   honest 503. Now superseded by the murakumo direction anyway.\n2. **No avatars** — the render canvas shows a placeholder box unless a visitor hand-types\n   a `?vrm=` URL param. Characters have no visual identity.\n3. **No character creation** — the roster is 4 hardcoded personas; there is no path for a\n   user to make their own character, which is also the missing supply side of\n   ADR-2607062200's creator-economy model (80/20 split needs creators).\n4. **The page reads as an engineering dashboard** — hero copy exists (PR #19), but the\n   dominant content is milestone status text and four audit ledgers.\n\n### Research grounding (verified this session)\n\n- **murakumo has two distinct live endpoints.** `api.murakumo.cloud/v1/messages`\n  (`local-murakumo`) is an Anthropic-Messages-API-shaped bridge to the *self-hosted*\n  `qwen-agentworld-35b-a3b` on the physical fleet (ADR-2607051431) — verified to never\n  touch an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`; caller auth is `ANTHROPIC_PROXY_TOKEN` (a murakumo-side\n  Worker secret; auth is a no-op if unset). `murakumo.cloud/api/v1/messages`\n  (`cloud-murakumo`/\"Sora\") is a *generic configurable reverse proxy* whose production\n  upstream is not verifiable from the repo. Precedent caller: `local-manimani`\n  (`manimani.kotodama-backend` via `langchain.model/anthropic-model` — standard Messages\n  JSON body, `x-api-key`/`anthropic-version` headers, nilable key).\n- **The avatar gap is plumbing, not architecture.** `network-isekai`'s `isekai.stage`\n  already runs the exact multi-avatar pattern needed (`avatar-cache` atom keyed by URL,\n  idempotent `ensure-avatar!`, per-frame draw of `:ready` entries); `babiniku.web` has the\n  single-shot MVP version of the same stack. Porting is ~40 lines plus a\n  register-callback indirection `babiniku.broadcast` already models.\n- **License-clear sample VRMs are scarce.** The VRM Consortium sample repo yields exactly\n  2 practical avatar models (Seed-san — already used — and VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample,\n  10.7 MB, both VRM Public License 1.0 / pixiv). Four distinct hardcoded avatars cannot be\n  sourced from it.\n- **The editor engine already exists** — `org-vrmc-vrm`'s restored\n  decompose/compose/export pipeline (ADR-2607071610 has the full inventory).\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. 完成系 defined — five capabilities, each with a \"done\" criterion\n\n| # | Capability | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| C1 | **Live chat** | A visitor sends a message and receives an in-character reply generated by murakumo's self-hosted model, gated by `review-turn`, in production |\n| C2 | **Live avatars** | Each roster character card shows/selects its own rendered VRM (no `?vrm=` param, no placeholder box as the default face of the product) |\n| C3 | **Character creation** | A visitor assembles a character in the kisekae flow, it persists (kotobase), and its avatar + persona join their roster and are chattable |\n| C4 | **Visitor-shaped LP** | First screen is product (hero → live character gallery → create-your-own entry → tiers), with containment transparency as a labeled trust section, not the page's dominant voice |\n| C5 | **Monetization** | UNCHANGED: honest HARD-hold until the etzhayyim rail matures (ADR-2607071000). The LP shows tiers as 準備中 — completion of *this* ADR does not require live payments |\n\n### 2. LLM backend: murakumo, `api.murakumo.cloud` (supersedes ADR-2607070800's model choice in part)\n\n- `functions/api/chat.js` retargets `https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1/messages`. The endpoint\n  is Anthropic-Messages-shaped, so the request construction survives; `MODEL` becomes the\n  fleet model id and the `@anthropic-ai/sdk` client gets `baseURL` pointed at the bridge.\n  **`murakumo.cloud/api/v1/messages` (Sora proxy) is explicitly rejected as the target**:\n  its upstream is operator-configurable and unverifiable — it *could* be pointed at real\n  Anthropic, which would silently violate the user's \"anthropic key はつかわずに\" intent.\n- Auth: a `MURAKUMO_PROXY_TOKEN` Cloudflare Pages secret, sent as the bridge's expected\n  token **iff the bridge's `ANTHROPIC_PROXY_TOKEN` is set** (open item: its production\n  state is unknown; if unset, auth is a no-op and chat works with zero secrets). Either\n  way the honest-default 503 pattern stays: unprovisioned/unreachable upstream must never\n  fabricate a reply.\n- **Structured outputs are unverified on the bridge.** ADR-2607070800's design leaned on\n  `output_config.format`; a Messages-*shaped* bridge to a qwen model may ignore it.\n  Design: keep sending the schema (harmless if ignored), add an explicit\n  produce-only-this-JSON instruction to the system prompt, parse defensively, and rely on\n  the unchanged `review-turn` gate — a malformed emotion/motion-cue already HARD-holds,\n  and the transcript already renders holds honestly. Verification is the first live call\n  after retargeting; if the model can't hold the JSON contract acceptably, the fallback\n  (decided then, not now) is a murakumo-side response-shaping layer, not a client hack.\n- ADR-2607070800 is superseded **only** in provider/model choice; everything else it\n  decided (server-side call boundary, persona system prompts, schema-mirrors-governor\n  vocabulary, honest-default, no self-fine-tune *in babiniku itself*) carries forward.\n\n### 3. Per-character live avatars\n\n- `babiniku.character/roster` gains `:vrm-url` per character.\n- `babiniku.web` ports `isekai.stage`'s `avatar-cache`/`ensure-avatar!` (keyed by URL,\n  `:loading/:ready/:error`), exposes `select-avatar!` through the same register-callback\n  indirection `babiniku.broadcast` uses, and the draw loop renders the selected\n  character's `:ready` parts (placeholder box only while nothing is ready).\n- UI: selecting a character (clicking its card / focusing its chat input) dispatches the\n  avatar swap. GPU-buffer disposal for swapped-out avatars is explicitly deferred\n  (network-isekai's own precedent) — low-frequency swaps, acceptable leak, follow-up.\n- **Avatar content**: Seed-san + VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample cover 2 slots today; the\n  other 2 characters share a placeholder until kisekae-produced avatars fill them. That\n  scarcity is *why C3 matters*: user-created avatars are the durable, license-clean\n  supply (the creator sets the meta/license at export — `kisekae.build/apply-meta`).\n\n### 4. Character creation via kisekae (ADR-2607071610)\n\n- babiniku embeds the kisekae flow (\"Create your character\"): pick base → swap parts →\n  recolor → name/license → save. The flow's UI composes `kotoba-lang/canvaskit`\n  (viewport), `kami-webgpu` (live preview through the same avatar-cache), and\n  `kotoba-lang/editor` (walk-the-spec controls) around the kisekae domain library.\n- Persistence: character specs via `kisekae.store`'s contract — `MemSpecStore` (browser\n  session) first, kotobase-backed store as the follow-up wiring, with user identity via\n  the actor-key CACAO self-mint convention (`manifest/repos.edn` `:kotoba`) when accounts\n  arrive. The spec (small EDN) is the artifact; the `.vrm` is derived — this is the\n  kotobase-datomic story the user's directive names.\n- Created characters register into the visitor's roster with a default persona template\n  (bio/speech-examples editable — text fields on the same spec), making them chattable\n  through the identical governor-gated pipeline. Creator-economy hook: a created\n  character is a creator asset; when the etzhayyim rail matures, ADR-2607062200's 80/20\n  applies to it with no new design.\n\n### 5. LP structure (C4)\n\nOrder: hero (exists) → **character gallery** (live avatar + tagline + \"chat\" per\ncharacter; the render canvas becomes the gallery's stage rather than a dead half-page) →\n**\"Create your character\"** entry → **tiers** (準備中, honest) → **\"How containment\nworks\"** — the ledgers/pending-escalation panels moved under a labeled trust section with\none paragraph of framing. Nothing is deleted: containment transparency is a deliberate,\nrepeatedly-reaffirmed design choice; this re-frames it as the differentiator it is instead\nof the landing experience.\n\n### 6. Out of scope, unchanged\n\nMonetization capability (HARD-held, ADR-2607071000), the NSFW-tier decision\n(ADR-2607062200 #5), shinshi.club (other agent), giemon embodiment scope (ADR-2607062210),\nand `babiniku.net` DNS (still blocked on a dashboard action or DNS-scoped token).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Implementation order (each its own PR series): **M4** murakumo chat live (retarget +\n  secret decision + first live verification incl. the structured-output question) → **M5**\n  avatars (roster `:vrm-url` + stage port) → **M6** kisekae flow embed (MemSpecStore first,\n  kotobase follow-up) → **M7** LP restructure. M4 and M5 are independent and can land in\n  either order.\n- Open items carried: murakumo bridge's `ANTHROPIC_PROXY_TOKEN` production state; the\n  qwen model's JSON-contract fidelity; 2 missing character avatars until kisekae supplies\n  them; kotobase-backed SpecStore + account identity.\n- `net-babiniku` gains dependencies on `kotoba-lang/kisekae`, `canvaskit`, and\n  `kotoba-lang/editor` when M6 lands (all sibling `:local/root`, the existing convention).\n- ADR-2607070800 amended in place (provider superseded, boundary design retained).\n\n### Addendum (2026-07-08): \"2 missing character avatars\" closed — Rin and Mei get\nreal composed avatars, plus a real VRM license-credit compliance gap fixed\n\nM6's compose engine (ADR-2607071610, shipped and verified live) closes this open\nitem without any new third-party asset: Rin and Mei now get real avatars **composed\nfrom the same two already-licensed VRM Consortium sample files** Aoi/Yui already\nuse (`jk-luxury/net-babiniku#39`) — Rin = VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample's body with\nSeed-san's hair+outfit; Mei = Seed-san's body/outfit with VRM1_Constraint_Twist_\nSample's hair+face (Twist-Sample has no separate `:outfit` category to donate).\n\n**License basis checked directly against both files' embedded `VRMC_vrm.meta`, not\nassumed**: both declare `modification: \"allowModificationRedistribution\"`,\n`avatarPermission: \"everyone\"`, `allowRedistribution: true` under VRM Public\nLicense 1.0 — composing/remixing parts between them is explicitly within license\nterms. This also surfaced a real, previously-missing compliance gap: Seed-san's\n`creditNotation` is `\"required\"` (credit VirtualCast, Inc.), but nothing in the app\ncredited it anywhere for Aoi's existing avatar either. Every built-in character now\ncarries `:avatar-credit`, rendered unconditionally and visibly on its card.\n\nA new `:avatar-spec` field (built-in characters only, distinct from user-created\ncharacters' `:kisekae/spec`) keeps `character-card-view`'s `created?` check\ncorrectly scoped — Rin/Mei get real composed avatars without gaining the\nEdit/Export/Delete UI meant only for what a visitor actually created. Verified live\nin production: both avatars render as full, correctly-posed, distinct humanoids;\nno console errors; `nbb character`/`governor`/`monetization`/`embodiment`/`persona`\nall pass.\n\nRemaining open items unchanged: `MURAKUMO_PROXY_TOKEN` production state, `babiniku.net`\nDNS, kotobase-backed SpecStore + account identity.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Keep the direct Anthropic backend and just provision the key.** Rejected — explicit\n   user direction; also the key was never provisioned in three weeks of asking, while\n   murakumo is first-party infrastructure.\n2. **Target `murakumo.cloud/api/v1/messages` (Sora proxy) since the user's words name that\n   domain.** Rejected as *primary* — its upstream is unverifiable from the repo and could\n   be real Anthropic, silently defeating the directive's intent; `api.murakumo.cloud` is\n   the verified self-hosted path. Recorded so the choice is reviewable.\n3. **Buy/commission 4 avatar files instead of building creation.** Rejected as the\n   *systemic* answer — it fixes 4 slots once, leaves user-generated characters (the\n   creator-economy supply) unsolved, and re-imports license risk kisekae's meta stamping\n   avoids.\n4. **Strip the audit ledgers off the page for a \"clean\" LP.** Rejected — containment\n   transparency is a standing product decision (ADRs 2607062200/0001); re-framed and\n   repositioned instead.\n5. **Wait for accounts/auth before any character creation.** Rejected — MemSpecStore\n   gives a real, honest single-session creation experience now; kotobase persistence is\n   additive wiring behind an already-tested contract.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607071610 (`kotoba-lang/kisekae` — the editor library this service consumes)\n- ADR-2607070800 (LLM backend — provider choice superseded here, boundary design retained)\n- ADR-2607051431 (`orgs/gftdcojp/local-murakumo` — the api.murakumo.cloud bridge),\n  ADR-2607041302 (murakumo family naming); `orgs/gftdcojp/local-manimani/src/manimani/kotodama_backend.clj`\n  + `orgs/kotoba-lang/langchain/src/langchain/model.cljc` (precedent caller shape)\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/network-isekai/src/isekai/stage.cljc` (`avatar-cache`/`ensure-avatar!` —\n  the avatar plumbing to port)\n- ADR-2607062200 / ADR-2607071000 (creator monetization + crypto rail — the unchanged\n  honest-default this design plugs into)\n- `vrm-c/vrm-specification` samples (the 2 license-clear VRMs; scarcity motivating C3)"), (:adr/decision "{:completion_criteria [{:id :c1, :capability \"live chat\", :done \"visitor sends a message, receives an in-character reply from murakumo's\\n           self-hosted model, gated by review-turn, in production\"} {:id :c2, :capability \"live avatars\", :done \"each roster character shows/selects its own rendered VRM; no ?vrm= param, no\\n           placeholder box as the product's default face\"} {:id :c3, :capability \"character creation\", :done \"visitor assembles a character via kisekae, it persists, its avatar+persona\\n           join their roster and are chattable\"} {:id :c4, :capability \"visitor-shaped LP\", :done \"first screen is product (hero -> gallery -> create -> tiers); containment\\n           transparency is a labeled trust section, not the dominant voice\"} {:id :c5, :capability \"monetization\", :done \"UNCHANGED -- honest HARD-hold until etzhayyim rail matures (ADR-2607071000);\\n           tiers shown as 準備中; this ADR's completion does NOT require live payments\"}], :llm_backend {:target \"https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1/messages (local-murakumo)\", :rejected_target \"murakumo.cloud/api/v1/messages (Sora proxy) -- upstream operator-\\n                     configurable and unverifiable; could be real Anthropic, silently\\n                     violating the user's intent\", :auth \"MURAKUMO_PROXY_TOKEN Cloudflare Pages secret iff the bridge's\\n          ANTHROPIC_PROXY_TOKEN is set (production state unknown -- open item); if unset,\\n          auth is a no-op and chat works with zero secrets. Honest-default 503 stays.\", :structured_outputs \"UNVERIFIED on the bridge: keep sending output_config.format\\n                        (harmless if ignored) + explicit JSON instruction in the system\\n                        prompt + defensive parse + unchanged review-turn gate (malformed\\n                        emotion/motion-cue already HARD-holds). First live call after\\n                        retargeting is the verification; if the model can't hold the\\n                        contract, the fallback is a murakumo-side shaping layer, decided\\n                        then\", :supersedes \"ADR-2607070800's provider/model choice ONLY -- its boundary design\\n                (server-side call, persona prompts, schema-mirrors-governor vocabulary,\\n                honest-default, no self-fine-tune in babiniku) carries forward\"}, :avatars {:roster \":vrm-url per character\", :plumbing \"port isekai.stage's avatar-cache/ensure-avatar! into babiniku.web; expose\\n              select-avatar! via the babiniku.broadcast register-callback indirection;\\n              draw loop renders selected character's :ready parts\", :gpu_teardown \"explicitly deferred (network-isekai's own precedent) -- low-frequency\\n                  swaps, acceptable leak, follow-up\", :content \"Seed-san + VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample cover 2 slots; other 2 share a\\n             placeholder until kisekae-produced avatars fill them -- user-created avatars\\n             are the durable, license-clean supply (creator sets meta at export)\"}, :character_creation {:flow \"babiniku embeds kisekae: pick base -> swap parts -> recolor -> name/license ->\\n          save; UI composes canvaskit (viewport) + kami-webgpu (preview via the same\\n          avatar-cache) + kotoba-lang/editor (walk-the-spec controls) around the kisekae\\n          domain lib\", :persistence \"kisekae.store contract: MemSpecStore (browser session) first;\\n                 kotobase-backed store is follow-up wiring; identity via actor-key CACAO\\n                 self-mint convention when accounts arrive. Spec (small EDN) is the\\n                 artifact; .vrm is derived -- the kotobase-datomic story\", :creator_economy \"a created character is a creator asset; when the etzhayyim rail\\n                     matures, ADR-2607062200's 80/20 applies with no new design\"}, :lp_structure \"hero (exists) -> character gallery (live avatars; render canvas becomes\\n                 the gallery stage) -> create-your-character entry -> tiers (準備中,\\n                 honest) -> 'How containment works' labeled trust section (ledgers moved,\\n                 framed, NOT deleted)\", :out_of_scope \"monetization capability (HARD-held), NSFW-tier decision, shinshi.club\\n                 (other agent), giemon embodiment scope, babiniku.net DNS (still blocked\\n                 on user action)\"}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/problem "{:source \"user direction 2026-07-07: 'babiniku.net の lp なども含めて、サービスとして\\n           完成系を設計して...' + 'anthropic key はつかわずに murakumo.cloud を使って' +\\n           '単なる四角いオブジェクトしか表示されていない' -- confirmed 'do it'\", :gaps [\"no live LLM (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY never provisioned; now superseded by murakumo\\n          direction anyway)\" \"no avatars (placeholder box unless a visitor hand-types ?vrm=)\" \"no character creation (4 hardcoded personas; creator economy has no supply side)\" \"page reads as an engineering dashboard, not a product LP\"], :research {:murakumo \"two live endpoints: api.murakumo.cloud/v1/messages (local-murakumo,\\n              Anthropic-Messages-shaped bridge to self-hosted qwen-agentworld-35b-a3b,\\n              ADR-2607051431, auth = ANTHROPIC_PROXY_TOKEN worker secret, no-op if unset;\\n              verified zero ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) vs murakumo.cloud/api/v1/messages\\n              (cloud-murakumo Sora, generic reverse proxy, upstream unverifiable).\\n              Precedent caller: local-manimani via langchain.model/anthropic-model\", :avatars \"network-isekai's isekai.stage already runs the needed multi-avatar pattern\\n             (avatar-cache keyed by URL, ensure-avatar!, per-frame draw of :ready);\\n             babiniku.web has the single-shot MVP of the same stack -- port is ~40 lines\\n             + a broadcast-style register-callback\", :vrm_scarcity \"vrm-c/vrm-specification yields exactly 2 practical license-clear\\n                  avatars (Seed-san, VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample -- VRM Public License\\n                  1.0/pixiv); 4 distinct hardcoded avatars cannot be sourced from it\", :editor_engine \"org-vrmc-vrm already ships decompose/compose/export -- see\\n                   ADR-2607071610\"}}"), (:adr/alternatives "[{:option \"keep direct Anthropic and just provision the key\", :rejected_because \"explicit user direction; key was never provisioned across weeks of\\n                      asking while murakumo is first-party infrastructure\"} {:option \"target murakumo.cloud Sora proxy (the domain the user's words name)\", :rejected_because \"upstream unverifiable, could be real Anthropic -- silently defeats\\n                      the directive's intent; api.murakumo.cloud is the verified\\n                      self-hosted path\"} {:option \"buy/commission 4 avatar files instead of building creation\", :rejected_because \"fixes 4 slots once; leaves the creator-economy supply side unsolved\\n                      and re-imports the license risk kisekae's meta stamping avoids\"} {:option \"strip the audit ledgers for a clean LP\", :rejected_because \"containment transparency is a standing product decision; re-framed\\n                      and repositioned instead\"} {:option \"wait for accounts/auth before any character creation\", :rejected_because \"MemSpecStore gives an honest single-session experience now; kotobase\\n                      persistence is additive wiring behind a tested contract\"}]"), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607071600: net-babiniku 完成系 -- service completion design (LP, live\n          avatars, murakumo LLM, kisekae editor)"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))